Subject: [#94-1-685] LEGAL: An Inter-PPL proposal - RFD

Okay everybody, rip this to shreds!
*******************************************
               Poly-Centric Law and List Etiquette.
                    The InterPPL Charter v0.1

This charter defines the framework within which List justice PPLs
operate on the Extropians emailing list.

1)   Creating a PPL.  A PPL is created by having its charter approved
     by ExI.  A PPL's charter must state:
     -    the PPL Head, whether individual or collective, with a single
          contact email address
     -    the procedures for joining and leaving, including any
          restrictions on membership (which may be arbitrary)
     -    the etiquette expected of its clients
     -    the procedures (which may be arbitrary) for handling charges
          brought by one client against another client, including an
          indication of the possible punishments (which may be
          arbitrary), but must include expulsion in extreme cases
     -    that it will observe the InterPPL Charter

2)   Changing a PPL's charter.  All changes require the approval of ExI.

3)   Inter-PPL charges.  A charge raised by a client against a client
     in another PPL is channelled through the PPL Head.  Charges are
     passed between PPLs via the PPL Heads, who each check that the
     charges are valid against their own respective PPL's charter. 
     Invalid charges are removed.  The surviving charges, if any, are
     processed by the defendant's PPL(s) in accordance with its own
     charter, as if they had been raised internally.  The defendant's
     PPL acknowledges membership to the plaintiff's PPL

4)   Outlaws.  An Outlaw is a list member not in any PPL.  If a PPL
     brings charges against an Outlaw (no PPL acknowledges ownership)
     they are reported to the List Administrator for an immediate
     posting ban, revoked only when a PPL accepts the Outlaw as client.

5)   Multiple Memberships.  A List member may be client of any number
     of PPLs

6)   Rogue PPLs.  A Rogue PPL is a PPL that no longer follows its
     charter.  Rogue PPLs may have their charter revoked by the ExI
     board a week after ExI publicly posts its grievances with a LEGAL
     prefix.
**********************************************
Notes:

I tried to keep this as simple as possible.  No fancy tech required!

PPL punishments on perps may include reporting to the List Administrator
for posting bans or enforced moderation, although it would be hoped that
PPLs, via their charters, would seek primarily to enforce behaviour by
consent through ultimate threat of expulsion.

Multiple memberships will be self-limiting through exposure to multiple
posting etiquettes.  Also individual PPLs may exclude clients with other
PPL affiliations under their membership restrictions.  Whether or not
a plaintiff's PPL will seek to pursue actions through multiple PPLs
depends on its charter.

There is no requirement for intra-PPL adjudicators, although some PPLs
may specify them.  Clients unhappy with the nature of a PPL's justice
vote with their feet.  ExI only has to be involved in creating, changing
and winding up PPLs. 

In the InterPPL charge filtering and distribution process no assessment
is made as to the defendants guilt, merely whether the charges are in
accordance with each PPL's charter.

The charges that any two list members can file against each other are
symmetric or reflexive.

Those with a more liberal posting etiquette have a more restricted
ability to bring charges.

There is no appeal against ExI's identification of Rogue PPLs, but ExI's
reputation would suffer accordingly if widely perceived false charges
were pursued without public discussion.   ExI may wish to consider the
creation of an Inter-PPL Adjudicator who would solely hear appeals from
clients/PPLs about possible Rogue PPL behaviour to bring them to the
attention of the PPL Heads and, if not acted upon, ExI.

